if you have

```C
void func(int x) {
test(x);
}
```

func receives x in r3 and test receives its first parameter in r3 so func doesn’t need to emit anything for parameters when calling test

if it was
```
void func(int x) {
test(0, x);
```

x needs to be moved to r4 as r4 is the 2nd argument of a function and 0 needs to be loaded in r3

